## 3. Language & Fixed Process Contract (`RS8`, `RS9`)

- **Document vs code language (`RS8`):** Write user-facing documents (`requirements.md`, questions, summaries) in **{{team_language}}**. Keep code identifiers, API routes, database fields, and symbol names in **English** exactly as written in the codebase.
- **Fixed process unchanged (`RS9`):** All `grilling` laws (draft first, confirm every inference, 0 open `Q-NN` before Gate 1, one question at a time), `gate-review` spec-mode steps, and `requirements.md` / `codebase-notes.md` / `change-impact.md` validated sections remain unchanged. Never add an `Assumptions` section; any unconfirmed fact is recorded as an `OPEN` `Q-NN` in `codebase-notes.md`.

